---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Almanac" description="Things Cail Daley makes outside the research papers: tools for scientific pipelines and agent orchestration, and dated writing on AI and science." mode="blended">
  <h1>Almanac</h1>
  <p class="intro">What I make around the science: the tools I build to get the work done, and writing on what changes when machines start doing science too.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Tools &amp; infrastructure</h2>
    <ul class="entries">
      <li><a href="https://cailmdaley.github.io/felt/">felt</a> — searchable, connected Markdown notes that keep decisions and context across agent sessions.</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/cailmdaley/shuttle">Shuttle</a> — agent orchestration across machines and HPC centres, with written tasks and a board for following the work.</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/cailmdaley/hark">hark</a> — live meeting transcription with speaker labels, written to a file an agent can follow.</li>
      <li><a href="https://unions-wl.github.io/production/status.html">UNIONS production dashboard</a> — live progress of DR6 full-footprint shape-catalogue production.</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/CosmoStat/shapepipe">ShapePipe</a> &amp; <a href="https://github.com/CosmoStat/sp_validation">sp_validation</a> — contributions to CosmoStat's galaxy-shape measurement and weak-lensing catalogue validation pipelines.</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/LightconeResearch">Lightcone Research tools</a> — open-source tools for verifiable AI-mediated science, built with the core team.</li>
      <li><a href="https://github.com/cailmdaley/unions-bmodes-mystra">UNIONS B-mode MySTRA report</a> — a public report mirror for the agent-produced B-mode validation paper.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Writing</h2>
    <ul class="entries dated">
      <li>
        <time datetime="2025-12-05">Dec 2025</time>
        <span><a href="/almanac/science-ai">Science &amp; AI</a> — what happens when machine scientific output exceeds human verification, with an interactive graph of epistemic claims.</span>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-xs);
  }

  .intro {
    text-indent: 0;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  section {
    margin: 0;
  }

  section + section {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-top: 0;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .entries {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .entries li {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .dated li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5.5rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--space-sm);
    align-items: baseline;
  }

  .dated time {
    font-variant-caps: all-small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-variant-numeric: lining-nums tabular-nums;
  }
</style>
